{
  "abstract": "We study the ordered entry surface of the four completions supplied by the order-three Diophantine-triple condition. Building on the four-regular-quintuple and one-square observation of kiro_septuple, we identify its function field explicitly with the elliptic fibration $v^2=\\kappa(t)^2r^2-2(r+2)^3$, where $\\kappa(t)=2(t^2+t+1)^3/[t(t+2)(2t+1)(t^2-1)]$. The base parameter is rationally recoverable from the ordered entries. The proof identifies individual quartic-root lifts with elliptic duplication and exhibits an involution fixing every entry. Its quotient has genus one, while retaining the signed root $p^2=ab+1$ gives genus-five fibres, with remaining equation $d^2=(r+2)^3(r-6)+16\\kappa(t)^2$. We give a rational decoder and an exact degree-two identification with the published Dujella–Peral full $2$-by-$6$ torsion family. A minimal Weierstrass model has six $I_6$ and six $I_2$ fibres and Kodaira dimension one. The one-square lift is independently certified by a determinant-one incidence minor and explicit multiplicative root formulas on the nonzero-radicand open set; a direct boundary argument shows that zero edges force collisions on this source. Two published zero-entry controls are checked by independent exact rational arithmetic. The contribution is the ordered entry/root dictionary and its geometric distinction, not a new torsion family. No new admissible sextuple or septuple, and no global nonexistence result, is claimed.",
